  "term": "ABR",
  "definition": "ABR, or auditory brainstem response, is an objective neurological test that measures how the auditory nerve and brainstem pathways respond to sound. It is used to assess hearing-related nerve pathways and to help identify suspected abnormalities involving the eighth cranial nerve and related auditory pathways.",
